From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Place VP9's low 2 bits plane by the frame
 height

The engine finds a 10-bit reference's low 2 bits plane after its chroma
plane at the frame's height, not the picture buffer's padded one. The
driver placed it after the padded chroma plane, so a frame whose height
is not a multiple of 16 wrote the plane where its next frame did not
read it: every inter frame of 1920x1080 VP9 profile 2 came out wrong,
key frames and 1088 or 1072 lines exact.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vp9.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vp9.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vp9.c
index d5155577c..5d8b9d038 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vp9.c
@@ -1042,9 +1042,8 @@ static int cedrus_vp9_job_configure(struct cedrus_context *ctx)
 	if (dec->bit_depth > 8 && !afbc) {
 		struct v4l2_pix_format fmt = cedrus_picture_recon_format(ctx);
 		u32 stride = fmt.bytesperline;
-		u32 h = fmt.height;
 		u32 stride2 = ALIGN(stride >> 2, 32);
-		u32 off = (u32)(chroma - luma) + stride * (h >> 1);
+		u32 off = (u32)(chroma - luma) + stride * (cur_h >> 1);
 		u32 cfg = VE_DEC_VP9_10BIT_CFG_STRIDE(stride2);
 
 		if (p010)
-- 
